From: Kristjan Sillmann <kristjan.h.s@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mic-stream

vic-anim streams the wake word's processed mic audio to the PC (plan 2026-11-08-mic-stream M4, T1, G1, P1,
C1-C5). ProcessTriggerLoop taps each 10 ms processedAudio block beside job->CollectProcessedAudio (no
MicDataInfo job: HasStreamingJob stays false, "Hey Vector" keeps working). Console var
MyVector_MicStreamPort (MicData, default 0): 0 = one atomic load per block, nothing else; non-zero = the
robot dials raw TCP to the IPv4 host of /data/data/myvector-voice.json's url (patch 0010) on that port.
G1: blocks pass only while the raw DoSVad flag is on (before the robot-noise force and the 1 s
QuietTimeCooldown), with 300 ms pre-roll and 400 ms hangover; P1: hangover + the PC's 300 ms GapCut = the
700 ms pause cut. C3: a 2 s ring the trigger loop never blocks on, drained by thread MyVectorMicTx
(pthread_create: -fno-exceptions, a failure leaves the stream off); a stall drops the oldest, logged at
most once a minute. C4: raw s16 16 kHz mono, one send() per 100 ms; keepalive 5+3x2 s and TCP_USER_TIMEOUT
3 s end a half-open socket, 2 s without send progress closes it; redial after a 1-30 s backoff that
doubles per loss and resets only after a 10 s connection (a PC close is seen while idle); an off -> on
port flip redials at once. C5: MyVectorMicTx runs nice 10 on cores 0+3 (MicProcRaw pins 2, MicProcTrigger
1). Logs my-vector.MicStream. Host test: robot/firmware/tests/mic-stream.sh.
